   "why": "26 of the 27 lines are read and sum to 23; line 5 is illegible under a crease and is null. The enumerator's footing of 25 leaves a residual of exactly 2 and there is exactly one unread cell for it to sit in - so the column is one legible cell away from closing, and 2 is what the sheet's own arithmetic asks of line 5. That is NOT written into the record: an arithmetic implication is not a reading, and the project's rule is that a column commits only when the lines READ sum to the footing. The column is therefore uncommitted, with its residual named and located."
